Template: tapir/site_url
Type: string
Default: http://localhost:8000
Description: Public URL of Tapir:
 The address members use to reach Tapir, e.g. https://tapir.example.org.
 The host name is also used as ALLOWED_HOSTS.

Template: tapir/database_auto
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Create the PostgreSQL database automatically?
 If PostgreSQL runs on this machine, the package can create a "tapir" role
 and database with a random password. Choose no to use an existing database.

Template: tapir/database_url
Type: string
Default: postgresql://tapir:CHANGE_ME@localhost:5432/tapir
Description: Database connection URL:
 Format: postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/DATABASE. Special characters in
 the password must be URL-encoded (e.g. @ as %40).

Template: tapir/redis_url
Type: string
Default: redis://localhost:6379
Description: Redis URL for celery:

Template: tapir/keycloak_setup
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Set up Keycloak on this machine?
 Runs tapir-setup-keycloak: Keycloak as podman container (systemd unit
 tapir-keycloak) with its own PostgreSQL database, the realm "tapir" for the
 public URL, the Keycloak login under the public URL in nginx, and Tapir
 connected to it. Choose no to use an existing Keycloak.

Template: tapir/keycloak_port
Type: string
Default: 8800
Description: Local port for Keycloak:
 Keycloak listens on 127.0.0.1 only; nginx forwards the login pages.

Template: tapir/admin_email
Type: string
Default:
Description: E-mail address of the first Tapir admin:
 Gets a Keycloak login; the initial password is written to
 /root/tapir-initial-admin.txt. Leave empty to skip.

Template: tapir/keycloak_admin_url
Type: string
Default: http://localhost:8080
Description: Keycloak URL used by the server:
 Internal address under which Tapir reaches the Keycloak admin API.

Template: tapir/keycloak_proxy
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Serve the Keycloak login under the public URL of Tapir?
 The generated nginx site then forwards /realms/ and /resources/ to the
 internal Keycloak address, and the public Keycloak URL is the public URL of
 Tapir. Keycloak needs KC_HOSTNAME set to that URL and KC_PROXY_HEADERS=xforwarded.
 Choose no if Keycloak has its own host name.

Template: tapir/keycloak_public_url
Type: string
Default: http://localhost:8080
Description: Public Keycloak URL:
 Address of Keycloak as seen by members' browsers.

Template: tapir/keycloak_realm
Type: string
Default: tapir
Description: Keycloak realm:

Template: tapir/keycloak_client_id
Type: string
Default: tapir-backend
Description: Keycloak client ID:

Template: tapir/keycloak_client_secret
Type: password
Description: Keycloak client secret:
 Leave empty to keep the current value.

Template: tapir/gunicorn_bind
Type: string
Default: 127.0.0.1:8000
Description: Address the web server listens on:
 Put a reverse proxy (nginx, caddy) with TLS in front of it. If nginx is
 installed, the package writes a matching site to
 /etc/nginx/sites-available/tapir; enabling it is left to you.

Template: tapir/tls_certificate
Type: string
Default:
Description: TLS certificate (full chain) for the nginx site:
 Leave empty for /etc/letsencrypt/live/<host>/fullchain.pem. As long as the
 file does not exist, the site only serves HTTP (enough to request a
 certificate); run "dpkg-reconfigure tapir" afterwards to switch to HTTPS.

Template: tapir/tls_certificate_key
Type: string
Default:
Description: TLS private key for the nginx site:
 Leave empty for /etc/letsencrypt/live/<host>/privkey.pem.
